# CHICKEN TIKKA MASALA
## info  
* About 40 minutes prep, 45 minutes total
* about 4 servings  

## ingredients
* 1/2 teaspoon ground cumin
* 1/2 teaspoon ground coriander
* 1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper
* 1 teaspoon table salt
* 2 pounds boneless, skinless chicken breasts
* 1 cup plain whole-milk yogurt
* 2 tablespoons vegetable oil
* 2 medium garlic cloves, minced or pressed (about 2 teaspoons)
* 1 tablespoon grated fresh ginger
* 3 tablespoons vegetable oil
* 1 medium onion, diced fine (about 1 1/4 cups)
* 2 medium garlic cloves, minced or pressed (about 2 teaspoons)
* 2 teaspoons grated fresh ginger
* 1 serrano chile, ribs and seeds removed, flesh minced
* 1 tablespoon tomato paste
* 1 tablespoon garam masala
* 1 (28 oz) can crushed tomatoes
* 2 teaspoons sugar
* table salt
* 2/3 cup heavy cream
* 1/4 cup chopped fresh cilantro leaves

## steps  
1. Combine cumin, coriander, cayenne, and salt in a small bowl.
1. Sprinkle both sides of the chicken with the spice mixture, pressing gently so the mixture adheres.
1. Place chicken on a plate, cover with plastic wrap, and refrigerate for 30-60 minutes.
1. In a large bowl, whisk together yogurt, oil, garlic, and ginger; set aside.
1. Heat oil in a large Dutch oven or large pan over medium heat until shimmering.
1. Add onion and cook, stirring frequently, until light golden, 8-10 minutes.
1. Add garlic, ginger, chile, tomato paste, and garam masala; cook, stirring frequently, until fragrant, about 3 minutes.
1. Add crushed tomatoes, sugar, and 1/2 teaspoon salt; bring to a boil.
1. Reduce heat to medium-low, cover, and simmer for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally.
1. Stir in cream and return to a simmer.
1. Remove the pan from heat and cover to keep warm.
1. While the sauce simmers, adjust the oven rack to the upper-middle position (about 6 inches from the heating element) and heat the broiler.
1. Using tongs, dip the chicken into the yogurt mixture so it is coated with a thick layer of yogurt, then arrange the pieces on a wire rack set in a foil-lined rimmed baking sheet or broiler pan.
1. Discard excess yogurt mixture.
1. Broil the chicken until the thickest parts register 160°F on an instant-read thermometer and the exterior is lightly charred in spots, 10-18 minutes, flipping halfway through cooking.
1. Let the chicken rest 5 minutes, then cut it into 1-inch chunks and stir into the warm sauce (do not simmer the chicken in the sauce).
1. Stir in cilantro, adjust seasoning with salt, and serve.

## notes  
* Use whole-milk yogurt and heavy cream for a rich, silky sauce.
* Broiling the chicken gives it a slightly charred exterior without drying it out.

## based on  
* Original recipe adapted from chicken tikka masala cooking techniques.
